<article class="env-lemma" id="0GQC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GQC">Lemma <span data-tag="0GQC">96.14.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{X} \to (\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ be a category fibred in groupoids which is representable by an algebraic space $F$. If $\mathcal{F}$ is in $\textit{LQCoh}(\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X})$ then the restriction $\mathcal{F}|_{F_{\acute{e}tale}}$ (<a href="/tag/075K" data-tag="075K">96.10.2.1</a>) is quasi-coherent. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U$ be a scheme étale over $F$. Then $\mathcal{F}|_{U_{\acute{e}tale}} = (\mathcal{F}|_{F_{\acute{e}tale}})|_{U_{\acute{e}tale}}$. This is clear but see also Remark <a href="/tag/0GQA" data-tag="0GQA">96.10.2</a>. Thus the assertion follows from the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>